Description: Akari OS desktop: akari with its apps, fonts and cursors
 Everything a machine needs to be an Akari OS desktop: akari and
 akari-shell, the display stack for Linux apps (TigerVNC, matchbox),
 Firefox ESR, fonts with CJK, network tools, and the guest tools for
 QEMU/KVM, VMware and Hyper-V, which only start on their own hypervisor.
 .
 It also has the Akari cursor theme for X, made from the same pictures the
 browser shows, and makes it the default.

Package: akari-shell
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         zsh,
         zsh-autosuggestions,
         zsh-syntax-highlighting,
         fastfetch,
         fontconfig
Description: zsh as Akari OS sets it up: oh-my-zsh, powerlevel10k, fastfetch
 The shell of Akari OS, for the terminal in the browser and for ssh:
 oh-my-zsh and powerlevel10k on fixed versions, read-only in /usr/share,
 with gitstatusd for git in the prompt; the font MesloLGS NF that
 powerlevel10k is made for, the Akari Symbols font, and fastfetch with the
 Akari logo in the account's accent colour.
 .
 New accounts get a ~/.zshrc that loads it (/etc/skel/.zshrc).
